NAME
====

**wattle-check** - compile a script without running it

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle check** [_options_] [_script_]

DESCRIPTION
===========

Compile _script_ without running it and report every error. With no _script_,
check standard input instead. The exit status is 0 after errors are reported,
unless **-b** is given. **c** is a synonym for ***check***.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-e**, **--lint-error** _level_:
  Set the lint level at which a message stops compilation with an error.
  _level_ is one of ``none``, ``relaxed``, ``normal``, ``strict`` or ``all``,
  written without a leading colon, or a number. These are the numbers 0, 1, 2
  and 3 and infinity. A message is reported when its own level is at most
  _level_, so ``none`` reports nothing and ``all`` reports every message. The
  default is ``none``.

- **-w**, **--lint-warn** _level_:
  Set the lint level at which a message is printed as a warning. _level_ takes
  the same values as for **-e**. The default is ``normal``.

- **-b**, **--bail**:
  Stop at the first error in the source and exit with status 1.

EXAMPLES
========

Check a script for compile errors without running it, stopping at the first:

````
$ wattle check --bail hello.wattle
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-test(1)`
